GATE NOTES (transparency — Honesty Covenant #9 no silent drift)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Module path: the prompt's gate text addresses `:app:`, but the Gradle module
   in this repo is `:android:` (settings.gradle.kts: include(":android"),
   projectDir=app; comment: "every P3/A* prompt gate addresses `:android:`").
   `:app:` does not resolve ("project 'app' not found"); the canonical
   `:android:` tasks were run instead — same build, correct module.
2. Execution mode: this is a SHARED runner; an external process repeatedly issued
   the Gradle daemon "stop command" mid-build ("Daemon is stopping immediately
   stop command received"), aborting daemon-backed runs at the final tasks.
   Re-run with `--no-daemon` (single-use JVM) completed cleanly. This changes only
   HOW the JVM is hosted, not WHAT is compiled/tested/linted.
3. Pre-existing repo conditions (NOT introduced by this artifact, NOT in this gate):
   - i18n catalog drift: `gen-i18n.ts --check` reports 11 generated files already
     drifted from web/src/i18n (en.json has 7796 grouped entries vs committed
     strings.xml 7779) BEFORE this change. A full regen is P1/S10 + cross-platform
     scope (also rewrites Apple/Windows). This artifact therefore added only its two
     required keys to the source (en.json) AND the three Android catalogs
     (values, values-ar, values-he) in sorted position — scoped, forward-stable.
   - `compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin` fails on OTHER surfaces' UI tests
     (BatteryCellsWidgetUiTest, DriveEfficiencyChartWidgetUiTest, ... 9 files) which
     carry an invalid `import androidx.compose.ui.test.assertExists` /
     `assertDoesNotExist`. The per-surface gate runs `testReleaseUnitTest`
     (JVM unit tests), which does NOT compile androidTest, so this is outside the
     gate. This artifact's ChargerTypeChartUiTest uses `.assertExists()` as a
     member call (no bad import), matching the working XRay/Sentry sibling pattern;
     it is NOT among the failing files and ktlint passed over the androidTest set.

